Now add the US-014 Playwright test to `scoring.spec.ts`. The test needs to click "Export PDF" and assert a download event fires. However, GAS web apps run in an iframe on `googleusercontent.com`, which means `URL.createObjectURL` won't trigger a `page.waitForEvent('download')` in Playwright. The download event in Playwright is only triggered by navigations to downloadable resources, not programmatic blob-URL clicks inside iframes.

The practical Playwright test for this case needs to watch for the toast message "ดาวน์โหลด PDF สำเร็จ" (confirming the server successfully generated the PDF and the client completed the download JS) rather than the actual download event, since the blob URL download inside an iframe won't fire Playwright's download event.

